asciinema plugin for DokuWiki

Share recorded terminal sessions created with asciinema.

All documentation for this plugin can be found at
https://www.dokuwiki.org/plugin:asciinema

If you install this plugin manually, make sure it is installed in
lib/plugins/asciinema/ - if the folder is called different it
will not work!

Please refer to http://www.dokuwiki.org/extensions for additional info
on how to install extensions in DokuWiki.

----
SYNTAX

  Local recording, played by the bundled JavaScript player:

    {{asciinema>linux.cast}}
    {{asciinema>wiki:demos:linux.cast}}

  Recording hosted on an asciinema server, embedded through its own script:

    {{asciinema>https://asciinema.org/a/569727}}

  Recording published as a plain .cast file on another site (the remote server
  must send CORS headers):

    {{asciinema>https://example.org/casts/demo.cast}}

  Alignment follows the usual DokuWiki media convention, using the spaces
  inside the curly braces:

    {{ asciinema>linux.cast}}     right
    {{asciinema>linux.cast }}     left
    {{ asciinema>linux.cast }}    centre

  A caption can be added after a pipe:

    {{asciinema>linux.cast|Booting a Linux kernel}}

OPTIONS

  Options are appended after a question mark and separated by "&". Flags may be
  written on their own or with an explicit value, e.g. "autoplay" or
  "autoplay=0".

    800x400           player size, also 800, 80% or a named size:
                      small, medium, large, half, full
    autoplay          start playing on page load
    loop              loop playback, loop=3 to repeat three times
    preload           fetch the recording on page load
    controls          always show the control bar, nocontrols to hide it
    speed=2           playback speed
    idle=2            shorten pauses longer than two seconds
    start=1:30        start playback at a given time, also startat= or t=
    theme=dracula     asciinema, dracula, gruvbox-dark, monokai, nord, seti,
                      solarized-dark, solarized-light, tango
    poster=npt:1:23   preview frame shown before playback
    cols=100&rows=30  terminal dimensions
    fit=width         width, height, both, or nofit for a fixed size font
    fontsize=big      small, medium, big or a CSS size, needs nofit
    font=Fira_Code    CSS font family, underscores become spaces
    lineheight=1.5    line height relative to the font size
    cursor=steady     blinking, steady or hidden
    keys              show the keystroke overlay
    pause             pause the playback on every marker

  Any flag can be negated with a "no" prefix: noautoplay, noloop, nopreload,
  nocontrols, nofit.

  Recordings embedded from an asciinema server are rendered by that server, so
  they only honour autoplay, loop, preload, speed, start, idle, theme, poster,
  cols and rows.

  Example:

    {{asciinema>linux.cast?800&theme=dracula&idle=2&poster=npt:0:15|Demo}}

UPLOADING RECORDINGS

  The plugin registers the "cast" extension as application/x-asciicast, which
  makes .cast files uploadable through the media manager. Turn the
  "register_mime" option off if you would rather declare the extension yourself
  in conf/mime.local.conf.

